# K04b (steps/callable-actual-projection-20260930.md, witness matrix row 3): the equivalent nullary
# actual FORMS in an argument position -- bare `task`, `task()`, `task: ()` -- carry the SAME receiving
# contract, the same descriptor, and the same absence of execution.  P0 keeps the atom and the nullary
# Frame apart (printTree: `recv (task)` is structure[atom "task"], `recv (task())` and `recv (task: ())`
# are one shape, structure[frame head="task" body=empty]); the receiving contract here is a callable
# formal, which receives the occurrence and does not execute it.  hits stays 0 through all three
# transports and becomes 1 only at the explicit invocation.  Success is 7.
int: hits 0

sub: task ()
    node\hits: node\hits + 1U
end: task

fn: count () int
    return: node\hits
end: count

fn: recv (task: f) int
    return: count()
end: recv

int: a recv(task)
int: b recv(task())
int: c recv(task: ())
int: after count()
if: a != 0 || b != 0 || c != 0
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 81; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
if: after != 0
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 82; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
task()
int: once count()
if: once != 1
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 83; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
